-- **An `or R` at an `impl fn` WITHOUT a result -- and it had no C at all until 2026-09-03.**
--
-- Two holes in one form, and the first hid the second. Both were measured on this file,
-- which `gabbro pruefe` has always accepted with `0 errors, 0 hints`:
--
--   1. **The CALL had no lowering.** `let … else` is the one form of error propagation this
--      language has (`SPRACHE.md` §8.1), and it pushed `&<binding>` for every callee that
--      does not return a GHOST -- then asked for the type of a result the declaration does
--      not have, and refused: *"`let … else` whose call has no resolvable type"*. The
--      declaration side had always known better: an `or R` function is `bool` in C and gets
--      a `*_wert` parameter **only when it has a result**. *The two halves of one lowering
--      disagreed about the same signature.*
--
--   2. **The SUCCESS return was never written.** A Gabbro function without a result carries
--      no closing `return`; C's `void` return is implicit. An `or R` function is `bool`, and
--      there the same body ran off the end of a non-void function -- the caller reads an
--      indeterminate value out of `if (!f(...))` and branches on it.
--
-- WHY NOBODY HAD SEEN IT
-- ----------------------
-- The corpus carried `or R` **exclusively at `extern fn`** -- foreign bodies this emitter
-- never sees -- until `messung/netz/udp-echo.gab`, and that one returns a VALUE on every
-- path, so the explicit `return <x>;` arm wrote the `return true;` for it. **A function with
-- an error channel and no result had no lowering to fall out of**, because hole 1 refused
-- every call to it one door earlier. *A defect behind a refusal is invisible for exactly as
-- long as the refusal stands.*
--
-- WHY THIS IS A CLEAN PROBE AND NOT A POISON
-- ------------------------------------------
-- A poison file needs a REFUSAL, and both refusals here were the bug. The counter-direction
-- that remains -- `let … else` over a callee that declares no `or <reason>` at all -- is
-- `N028`'s, and the checker says it BEFORE the emitter gets there; a poison on it would join
-- the ten already booked as *verdeckt* in `zaehle-gifttreffer.py` and raise a mark that is
-- meant to fall.
--
-- So the guard is the other one: **stage 9 of `pruefe-emission.sh` emits this file and hands
-- its C to `cc -Werror` at every run.** If hole 1 comes back, the file stops emitting and
-- `MARKE_EMIT_M` falls -- and that mark is read, not eyeballed.
--
-- > **And hole 2 has no reader at `cc` at all**, which is the sharper half of the finding:
-- > `-Wreturn-type` does not reach a `static` function nothing has called yet, so the missing
-- > `return true;` compiled clean at `-O0` and at `-O2`. **The only instrument that sees it
-- > is a RUN** -- `lauf "fragment1"` over `messung/fragmente/F01.gab`, whose first and
-- > last-but-one printed values are exactly the two success verdicts of an `or R` body.
-- > *A defect whose only witness is the execution is the reason `H` counts Durchstiche and
-- > not compilations.*

module proben::fehlerkanal_ohne_ergebnis {

reason R { Boese = 1 "der Zaehlerstand liegt ausserhalb 0 .. 100" exhaustive }

type Zelle = { n : u32, };

-- Ein Fehlerkanal OHNE Ergebnis: `bool tut_was(Zelle *, R *_grund)` -- kein `*_wert`.
impl fn tut_was(z : ptr<normal, rw> Zelle)
    or R
    effects { writes z }
    costs <= 8 ops
{
    narrow z.n to 0 .. 100 else { return R::Boese; }
    z.n += 1;
}

-- Der Ruf, und er ist die Form, die es bis zum 2026-09-03 nicht gab.
impl fn rufer(z : ptr<normal, rw> Zelle)
    or R
    effects { writes z }
    costs <= 20 ops
{
    let ok = tut_was(z) else (e) { return e; }
}

}
